🔢 Max Consecutive Ones

The goal is to find the maximum number of consecutive "1"s in a binary array.

- Traverse the array from left to right.
- If the current element is "1", increment the current consecutive count.
- If the current element is "0", reset the current count to "0".
- Keep track of the maximum count found so far.
- Return the maximum consecutive count.

Time Complexity: "O(n)"
Space Complexity: "O(1)"


###Solution

class Solution {
    public int findMaxConsecutiveOnes(int[] nums) {
        int count=0;
        int max=0;
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++)
        {
            if(nums[i]==1)
            {
               count++;
               max=Math.max(max,count);
            }
            
            else
            {
                count=0;
            }
        }
        return max;
    }
}
